<title>FRANCE: MATIF to cut commissions on euro-contracts.</title>
<headline>MATIF to cut commissions on euro-contracts.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>French futures and options exchange MATIF SA said on Friday it will cut the commission levied on contracts maturing after January 1, 1999 in a bid to improve its competitiveness in the battle for euro-denominated business.</p>
<p>MATIF said in a statement it would be cutting the levy on each lot traded to four francs from six. The commission on contracts maturing before January 1, 1999 will remain the same, it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
